1140-
1141-### 21.1 Lifecycle hooks (frozen)
1142-
1143-| phase | hook | when | failure policy |
1144-|---|---|---|---|
1145:| discover | *(none — filesystem scan)* | once per process, or on dev reload under `STS_WORKFLOW_DEV_RELOAD` | per-provider exclusion |
1146-| describe | `manifest()` | discovery | exclusion |
1147:| describe | `settings_schema()` | lazy, first request, memoized (`registry.py:107-117`) | returns `None`, WARN; provider still listed with `has_settings: false` |
1148-| configure | `validate_settings(settings) -> list[dict]` | on save, on select, on demand | exception → one redacted root `error` issue; raw exception is internal only |
1149-| probe | `health_check(settings) -> dict \| str \| HealthResult` | explicit user action or TTL cache (§21.5) | exception → `HealthResult(status="fail", message="Health check failed")`; raw exception is logged only after redaction |
1150:| construct | **`create() -> Provider`** (new v2 factory) | lazily, at first invocation | exception → `ProviderError` at the registry boundary (10.3); provider marked `degraded` |
1151:| serve | domain-specific invocation | per request | 10.3 |
1152-| bind | `register_runtime(app, sock)` | once at boot, `kind == "extension"` only | caught and logged (`runtime.py:63-65`); boot continues |
1153-| release | `shutdown()` | registry teardown, dev reload, process exit | best-effort; exceptions logged, never raised; **must be idempotent** |
1154-
1155:The v2 factory replaces the eight zero-argument `get_provider()` functions, none of which has
1156-ever executed (§14.1, §16). Frozen rules: `create()` is called **at most once per
1157:`(domain, provider_id)` per process**, through a per-provider construction lock, never at
1158:import time, and never during discovery — so importing a provider package can never start a
1159-model load, a thread, or a socket. Provider code is not called while the hub-wide registry
1160:lock is held. The invocation context frozen by 10.3 is passed to each domain invocation, **not
1161-to the memoized factory**; retaining the first request's project/output/cancellation context
1162:inside a process-wide provider would cross-contaminate later executions. Owner: **11.2**.
1163-
1164-`shutdown()` today exists on `Runtime` (`runtime.py:45-47`) and on `TTSProvider` with **zero
1165:callers**. v2 requires the registry to call it for every constructed provider on teardown, in
1166-reverse construction order. Owner: **11.2**.
