1168-### 21.2 Registration and discovery order (frozen)
1169-
1170-1. Domains initialize in `DOMAINS` declaration order: `script`, `scene_blueprint`, `tts`,
1171-   `storyboard`, `animator` — replacing the fixed three-call sequence at `app.py:90-95`.
1172:2. Within a domain, providers are loaded in **`sorted()` order of folder name**. Today
1173-   `os.listdir` order is used unsorted (`registry.py:239`); sorting is required so discovery
1174-   logs, catalog responses, and "first wins" duplicate resolution are deterministic.
1175-   Owner: **11.1**.
1176-3. Discovery is idempotent — a second `discover()` on a registry that already scanned is a
1177:   no-op (`<domain>/providers/__init__.py:20-23`). Dev reload explicitly resets the flag after
1178:   calling `shutdown()` on constructed providers.
1179:4. Extension runtimes bind after **all** domains have been discovered, never interleaved with
1180-   discovery, so a runtime can rely on the full catalog being present.
1181-5. Registration never touches `app.py` or `studio/workflows/registry.py`.
1182-6. Discovery and dev reload build a private catalog snapshot and publish it with one atomic
1183-   swap. Concurrent requests see either the complete old snapshot or the complete new one,
1184-   never a partially discovered catalog. Providers removed by the swap are shut down only
1185-   after new lookups can no longer acquire them and all pre-swap invocation leases have
1186:   drained; teardown must not close a provider still serving an old-snapshot request.
