1693-Frozen rules:
1694-
1695:- **`settings` vs `options`.** `settings` are the durable per-provider values from
1696-  `settings/settings.json` with the env read-time fallback already resolved; they may contain
1697-  secrets and must never be echoed into a result. `options` are the per-run values from the
1698:  node's `provider_options` / request body and must never contain secrets. A provider reads
1699-  both and writes neither. This split is what makes `job_meta.resolved_settings_redacted`
1700:  (`pipeline/services.py:166`, `:272`) mechanical rather than per-provider hand-work.
1701:- **No Flask, no `request`, no globals.** The context is the provider's only access to caller
1702:  state. A provider that needs `STS_PORT`, `flask.request`, or `os.environ` is non-conforming
1703-  (blockers B2 and B8).
1704-- **`cancel`, `progress`, and `log` are never `None`.** Today every consumer must write
1705-  `stop = context_value(context, "stop_requested"); if stop and stop():`
1706-  (`adapters/storyboard.py:47-48`, `adapters/animator.py:57-58`). v2 supplies no-op
1707:  implementations so a provider never guards. Owner: **11.4**.
1708:- **`attempt` is informational.** Retry is the caller's decision (§35.2); a provider must not
1709-  implement its own retry of a whole invocation on top of it.
