1934-Frozen rules:
1935-
1936:1. `len(units) == len(requested units)`. A unit the provider never attempted is
1937-   `state: "skipped"`, not an omission. Today a scene that never reports simply stays
1938-   `pending` in `scene_statuses` and the poll loop can only infer it by arithmetic
1939-   (`pending = total - ready - errors`, `pipeline/services.py:593`).
1940-2. `unit_index` is the caller's index (the scene `index`), so a partial re-run addresses the
1941-   same units. Positional inference is forbidden.
1942:3. Envelope `status` is derived, never provider-declared, in this precedence order:
1943-   any unit `cancelled` and no unit failed → cancel the invocation (even if an earlier unit
1944-   succeeded); otherwise all succeeded → `succeeded`; otherwise at least one succeeded →
1945-   `partial`; otherwise → `failed` (raised, §31.4). This ordering prevents a cancellation
1946-   arriving after one completed scene from being misreported as ordinary partial success.
1947:4. `artifact_refs` at envelope level is the ordered union of unit refs plus domain-level
1948-   artifacts (the manifest JSON). No unit-level ref may be missing from it.
1949-5. A `failed` unit must carry `error`; a `succeeded` unit must carry at least one
1950:   `artifact_ref` unless the domain declares otherwise.
1951-6. Unit `error.message` obeys §31.2. This closes the current leak at
1952-   `storyboard/routes.py:254`, where `"error": str(e)` writes raw exception text into
1953-   `storyboard.json`, which the storyboard adapter then hands to the `images` port verbatim
1954-   (`adapters/storyboard.py:46`).
1955-
1956:**Whether `partial` fails the node is the caller's policy, not the provider's.** Frozen
1957-default for workflow execution: `partial` succeeds the node and records a warning, matching
1958-today (a run with 9/10 images succeeds). 14.1 may add an opt-in per-node "require all units"
1959-setting; it must default off.
