2208-### 33.3 Poll and push (frozen)
2209-
2210-Providers declare exactly one of two delivery modes through capabilities (§20.4):
2211-
2212-- `async_job` without `push_callbacks` — the platform polls `poll(job_id, invocation)`.
2213:  Frozen cadence: first poll after 2 s, then the domain interval, ±10 % jitter. Domain
2214-  intervals are today's values: storyboard 10 s, animator 10 s
2215-  (`pipeline/services.py:573`, `:688`). A poll that raises is retried up to 3 consecutive
2216-  times before the job is failed; the current loop swallows *every* poll exception forever
2217:  (`pipeline/services.py:624-625`), which turns a permanently broken provider into a 30-minute
2218-  wait.
2219:- `push_callbacks` — the provider pushes status through its runtime (WebSocket for
2220-  `gemini_ws` / `grok_automa`, HTTP callback for `wavespeed_webhook`). The platform still
