2372-### 35.2 Retry and idempotency (frozen)
2373-
2374:- **The platform retries invocations; providers do not.** A provider may retry an internal
2375:  HTTP request only when it is read-only or carries a provider-supported idempotency key; it
2376-  must not blindly retry a generation `POST`, because a lost response can otherwise create
2377-  two remote jobs. Today's `call_webhook` retries every request 3 times / 2-4-8 s
2378-  (`webhooks.py:9-10`); 13.2/13.4 must either add an idempotency key for generation calls or
2379-  disable those internal retries before dispatch moves behind this boundary.
2380-- A retried invocation gets a **new** `invocation_id` and an incremented `attempt`. Any job
2381-  submitted by the failed attempt must be cancelled or abandoned before the retry; two live
2382:  jobs for one `(domain, project_id)` are a contract violation.
2383-- Retry is only safe because artifacts are staged: a failed attempt publishes nothing
2384-  (`promoter.promote()` runs only on success, `scheduler.py:728`).
2385:- For multi-unit domains, retry re-requests **only** units not in a terminal `succeeded`
2386-  state; already-produced artifacts are reused. This is 14.1's "restart reconciliation".
2387-- Non-retryable errors (§34.3) skip the remaining attempts.
