2525-Rules that bind all three:
2526-
2527:1. **No manual edits.** A workflow saved before the migration, a `settings.json` written before
2528:   the migration, a legacy `POST` body sent by a legacy page, and an execution/cache record on
2529-   disk must all keep working with zero user action. This is §17.1 restated as an executable
2530-   requirement; §48 makes it a test.
2531-2. **Upgrade is idempotent.** Running an upgrade twice equals running it once. Every upgrade
2532-   step below is specified so that re-running it on already-upgraded data is a no-op.
2533-3. **Upgrade is write-once and recorded.** Node-config upgrades land in
2534:   `extensions.type_version_migrations` (`migrations.py:15,125`); settings upgrades bump
2535-   `settings.json.version`. Nothing upgrades a document that is only being read.
2536:4. **Reject is never a fallback.** The current code silently substitutes a provider when the
2537-   requested one is unknown (`storyboard/routes.py:320-322`, `animator/schemas.py:36`,
2538:   `services.py:551`). Under v2 an unknown provider ID is a `PROVIDER_NOT_FOUND` error
2539-   (§34.2), except at the two documented alias boundaries in §40.3.
2540:5. **Support window.** Legacy request fields and legacy provider strings are supported until
2541-   step **16.1** removes the internal HTTP hop and the legacy pages that emit them. Persisted
2542-   shapes (settings, workflow JSON, execution/cache records) have **no** removal date: their
2543-   upgrade paths are permanent.
